    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented customerCode collision de-duplication in the V1 owner controller.\n\n**File changed:** `src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`\n\nThe `customerCode(Owner)` helper previously returned the raw `<REGION>-<HASH8>` code. It now:\n1. Computes the base code as before.\n2. Collects the `customerCode`s of all existing owners (via `clinicService.findAllOwners()`, filtering nulls \u2014 matching the pattern used by the other derived-attribute helpers).\n3. If the base code is free, returns it unchanged.\n4. Otherwise appends `-<n>`, starting at `n = 2` and incrementing to the smallest value that isn't already taken, and returns that de-duplicated code.\n\nThis runs inside `assignDerivedAttributes(...)`, which fires before `saveOwner`, so the new owner isn't yet persisted and can't collide with itself.\n\nI also added the two missing imports (`java.util.Objects`, `java.util.stream.Collectors`); `java.util.Set` was already present.\n\n**Tests:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the `AcceptanceTest`, the only test class in the project, which asserts distinct owners get distinct customerCodes).",
